In the sun-drenched jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, a tiny gnome warlock named Zippik the Unseen crept through the undergrowth, his glowing green eyes scanning for threats. His succubus, Lila, slinked beside him—elegant, graceful, her crimson eyes gleaming with mischief. “*They’re all so slow,*” she purred in his mind. “*Let me charm them.*”

Zippik grinned. “Just don’t flirt with the boss.”

Lila giggled as she approached a group of snarling boars. With a flick of her tail, she cast *Seduction*. The lead boar froze, eyes glazed, then began nuzzling her. The others paused, confused. Zippik unleashed a *Shadow Bolt*, and the charm held—until the boar, distracted by Lila’s purr, tripped over a root and fell into a pit trap.

“*Oops,*” Lila whispered.

Zippik laughed. “You’re trouble, but the best kind.”

They continued, Lila charming every enemy in sight—goblins, trolls, even a grumpy old druid. The questing was easy, the loot plentiful. But Zippik knew the truth: *Seduction* made her invisible to the world’s eyes. No one saw her. No one noticed the tiny gnome and his silent, charming companion. That was why she was everywhere—and yet, never truly seen.

**Answer:** The Succubus’s *Seduction* ability makes her invisible to enemies, allowing her to charm and bypass threats undetected—making her more effective and common in practice than appearances suggest. [end of text]


